</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Details on average costs, prompt and completion token usage per problem. For GPT-5/GPT-5 mini, costs reflect average measured per-run, which may reflect savings due to prompt caching. For open-weight models, estimates are based on pricing from available API providers and measured token usage.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For models run from API providers, we report an average of the actual cost of each run as calculated through API usage with <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">litellm</span> .
For open-weight models, we run original experiments on our own hardware, and report cost estimates based on token usage and pricing quoted from an appropriate provider.
<a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix D Run Cost Estimation ‣ Appendix C Case Study Details ‣ Appendix B Analyzing Results by SWE Difficulty ‣ Sampling Personas ‣ Appendix A User Simulation Details ‣ Dialogue-SWEBench: A Benchmark for Dialogue-Driven Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 8</span></a> lists the token usage across runs, API pricing, estimated or reported average cost, and the API provider.
The cost of user simulator inference is excluded from all runs.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Naturalness &amp; Coherence Human Ratings</h2>

<figure id="A5.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F12.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2606.13995v1/imgs/figs/plots/nat_coh_v2/naturalness_human_plot.png" id="A5.F12.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:448/347;" width="448" height="347" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Dialogue naturalness (human annotations)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F12.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2606.13995v1/imgs/figs/plots/nat_coh_v2/coherence_human_plot.png" id="A5.F12.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:448/347;" width="448" height="347" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Dialogue coherence (human annotations)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F12.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2606.13995v1/imgs/figs/plots/nat_coh_v2/naturalness_llm_plot_w_rules_gemma.png" id="A5.F12.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:448/347;" width="448" height="347" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Dialogue naturalness (LLM annotations)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F12.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2606.13995v1/imgs/figs/plots/nat_coh_v2/coherence_llm_plot_w_rules_gemma.png" id="A5.F12.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:448/347;" width="448" height="347" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>Dialogue coherence (LLM annotations)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>Human and LLM ratings for naturalness and coherence (1–3) with 95% confidence intervals for each system, evaluated on the human-annotated subset of the data (30 dialogues per agent-model pair)</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A5.F12.sf1" title="12(a) ‣ Figure 13 ‣ Appendix E Naturalness &amp; Coherence Human Ratings ‣ Appendix D Run Cost Estimation ‣ Appendix C Case Study Details ‣ Appendix B Analyzing Results by SWE Difficulty ‣ Sampling Personas ‣ Appendix A User Simulation Details ‣ Dialogue-SWEBench: A Benchmark for Dialogue-Driven Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12(a)</span></a> and <a href="#A5.F12.sf2" title="12(b) ‣ Figure 13 ‣ Appendix E Naturalness &amp; Coherence Human Ratings ‣ Appendix D Run Cost Estimation ‣ Appendix C Case Study Details ‣ Appendix B Analyzing Results by SWE Difficulty ‣ Sampling Personas ‣ Appendix A User Simulation Details ‣ Dialogue-SWEBench: A Benchmark for Dialogue-Driven Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12(b)</span></a> respectively present the results of our human annotation for the naturalness and coherence on 360 dialogues, as described in <a href="#S7" title="7 Analyzing Dialogue Quality ‣ Dialogue-SWEBench: A Benchmark for Dialogue-Driven Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§ 7</span></a>.
<a href="#A5.F12.sf3" title="12(c) ‣ Figure 13 ‣ Appendix E Naturalness &amp; Coherence Human Ratings ‣ Appendix D Run Cost Estimation ‣ Appendix C Case Study Details ‣ Appendix B Analyzing Results by SWE Difficulty ‣ Sampling Personas ‣ Appendix A User Simulation Details ‣ Dialogue-SWEBench: A Benchmark for Dialogue-Driven Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12(c)</span></a> and <a href="#A5.F12.sf4" title="12(d) ‣ Figure 13 ‣ Appendix E Naturalness &amp; Coherence Human Ratings ‣ Appendix D Run Cost Estimation ‣ Appendix C Case Study Details ‣ Appendix B Analyzing Results by SWE Difficulty ‣ Sampling Personas ‣ Appendix A User Simulation Details ‣ Dialogue-SWEBench: A Benchmark for Dialogue-Driven Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12(d)</span></a> present the LLM-as-a-judge results for the same <span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">human-annotated subset</span>.
While human annotators and our LLM-as-a-judge rank system naturalness identically, there are a few differences in ranking for system coherence. Notably, human coherence ratings rate schema-guided agent with GPT-5-mini highest, where the LLM-as-a-judge ranks it equal to or below other agents.</p>
</div>
